{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01FdefM8whsMvJzAf5csXEd6", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://repository.uin-suska.ac.id/58155/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.academia.edu/23400897\"}, {\"url\": \"https://journal.ugm.ac.id/jurnal-humaniora/article/download/693/539\"}, {\"url\": \"https://ojs.badanbahasa.kemdikbud.go.id/jurnal/index.php/kandai/article/download/320/139\"}, {\"url\": \"https://mailtrack.io/trace/link/7570b458e1d5448948ae3fd44d9a04085a0c72e6?\"}, {\"url\": \"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6549484W\"}, {\"url\": \"https://online-english.britishcouncil.org/direct-buzz/makassar-to-bugis-translation-a-simple-guide-1767647905\"}, {\"url\": \"https://luk.staff.ugm.ac.id/bahasa/2017-KemdikbudKamusBahasaBugis-Indonesia.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://pustaka.taratsa.id/download/5626/pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:15:30.326Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "bahasa Bugis \"naik\" menre' kamus", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_016sLRXt7nGRnUsEfbgy5QqY", "content": [{"title": "repository.uin-suska.ac.id", "url": "https://repository.uin-suska.ac.id/58155/"}, {"title": "www.academia.edu", "url": "https://www.academia.edu/23400897"}, {"title": "ugm.ac.id", "url": "https://journal.ugm.ac.id/jurnal-humaniora/article/download/693/539"}, {"title": "ojs.badanbahasa.kemdikbud.go.id", "url": "https://ojs.badanbahasa.kemdikbud.go.id/jurnal/index.php/kandai/article/download/320/139"}, {"title": "mailtrack.io", "url": "https://mailtrack.io/trace/link/7570b458e1d5448948ae3fd44d9a04085a0c72e6?"}, {"title": "pantek Kamus bahasa Bugis-Indonesia", "url": "https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6549484W"}, {"title": "Makassar To Bugis Translation: A Simple Guide", "url": "https://online-english.britishcouncil.org/direct-buzz/makassar-to-bugis-translation-a-simple-guide-1767647905"}, {"title": "2017 KemdikbudKamusBahasaBugis Indonesia", "url": "https://luk.staff.ugm.ac.id/bahasa/2017-KemdikbudKamusBahasaBugis-Indonesia.pdf"}, {"title": "pustaka.taratsa.id", "url": "https://pustaka.taratsa.id/download/5626/pdf"}]}, "The search didn't return a dictionary entry for *menre'* itself, but one source gives the general sense of the word.\n\n- **Meaning:** A Bugis-language article says that in common Bugis, the word menre or manai is used for the meaning 'up/rise'. The article also notes that the classical Bugis of the epic I Lagaligo uses a different form, *manerru*. Since *menre'* is the glottal-stopped spelling of *menre*, this is likely the same word, but the source doesn't say so directly.\n- **Dictionaries:** The Balai Bahasa Provinsi Sulawesi Selatan published a revised *Kamus Bahasa Bugis—Indonesia* in 2022, which lists Bugis headwords and sub-headwords (lema dan sublema bahasa Bugis). The search snippet doesn't show its entry for *menre'*. An earlier dictionary from 1977 (*pantek Kamus bahasa Bugis-Indonesia*) is also catalogued by Open Library.\n- **Regional variant:** A 2017 bilingual dictionary from the Kantor Bahasa NTB covers Bugis as spoken on Sumbawa, which may differ from the Sulawesi form.\n\nTo confirm the exact entry and its usage, check the 2022 Balai Bahasa dictionary, which is available as a PDF at pustaka.taratsa.id."], "durationSeconds": 5.720019250000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01FdefM8whsMvJzAf5csXEd6", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
